From 5276e9ae6a8e1d1222b9d0c59442a56ab47b7911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xs1128 <hipac1@lsalab.cs.nthu.edu.tw>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HLLC: reconstruct the WENO5 states in-kernel on the
 5-equation pure-fluid path

Each sweep wrote the WENO5 left/right states of every cell to qL/qR_rs*_vf (2 x sys_size values per cell) and the
HLLC kernel read them back. On the 5-equation pure-fluid path the HLLC kernel now reconstructs the two states of its
face itself, from q_prim, so neither buffer is written or read and s_reconstruct_riemann_states does nothing.

- The WENO5 point formula (smoothness indicators, then per boundary: polynomials, weights for WENO-JS/mapped/Z/TENO,
  value) moves to src/simulation/include/weno5_macros.fpp. s_weno and the HLLC kernel both expand it, so the
  in-kernel states are bitwise the ones s_weno stores. s_weno's second boundary still reuses tau/delta.
- HLLC emits its pure-fluid 5-equation kernel a third time (FUSED). The shared body reads its states through
  QL()/QR() accessors: buffer elements in the existing emissions, thread-private arrays in the fused one. The
  in-place mpp_lim clipping becomes thread-local; no other reader of the buffers exists on this path.
- Selected at init (recon_riemann_fused, m_rhs) when HLLC + 5-equation + WENO5 and nothing else reads or edits the
  buffers: flux_aliased (no viscous/capillary/chemistry/bubbles/IB/hypoelasticity/cylindrical), no mp_weno, THINC,
  weno_Re_flux, damage, MHD, IGR, no BC_RIEMANN_EXTRAP boundary, sys_size within the private-array bound.
- The cost is one extra smoothness-indicator evaluation per face (each cell's beta is computed for both of its faces);
  the weights, the expensive part, are computed once per side as before.

perf3d 201^3, 1 H200, same node (667981): 42.05 -> 37.75 ms/step (-10.2 %), bitwise vs v5.7.0.
